# The live project this repository is deployed against.
#
# Both values below are public by design: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the
# browser bundle, and Supabase's publishable key is meant to be shipped to
# clients — it is row-level security, not the key, that decides what anyone can
# read or write. That posture is tested (supabase/tests/rls.sql) and was checked
# against this project after it was seeded: an anonymous visitor can read the
# twelve farms and the reviews, and cannot read a booking, a profile or the
# farmer lead list, or write a booking.
#
# The service-role key and the Razorpay secret are NOT here and never should be.
# Set those as environment variables on the host (Vercel → Settings →
# Environment Variables); without them, admin approvals and card payments stay
# switched off and the rest of the site works.
#
# Rotate the publishable key from Settings → API in the Supabase dashboard if
# you would rather not carry it in git; the app falls back to demo mode without
# it rather than breaking.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://rzwzaytodauobtrmsfei.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_tCB_pfgFMsLlA2qHc4CyeQ_qhtAvvBM

NEXT_PUBLIC_ROOT_DOMAIN=connecttonature.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_HOST_SUBDOMAIN=shetkari
